    "qualifierLines": [
      "{**7 NY3d at 423} OPINION OF THE COURT",
      " I dissent reluctantly. The reasons that the majority gives for its holding are good ones, and I agree that the holding is supported, though not compelled, by our decisions in People v Williams (56 NY2d 236 [1982]) and People v Shields (46 NY2d 764 [1978]). But I cannot accept the proposition that an error that prevented a defendant from telling his side of the story to a jury can ever be \"harmless.\" "
